  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788612",
      "title": "Storing Data Models in Separate Files",
      "lectureOrder": 48,
      "videoOrder": 44,
      "sourceHash": "80954bd82ad40d101e27d7637258a9f05d8338ae0956d3cbae01a523f76ae5bd",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.768,
          "end": 2.88,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmüller] Now in the previous lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.88,
          "end": 6,
          "en": "I added this task interface here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6,
          "end": 9.333,
          "en": "this custom task type definition in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.32,
          "end": 13.32,
          "en": "And we did something similar earlier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.32,
          "end": 17.733,
          "en": "for the user type here in the user component file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.96,
          "end": 21.27,
          "en": "Now, whilst you can do it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.27,
          "end": 24.48,
          "en": "it is quite common in Angular apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.48,
          "end": 29.22,
          "en": "to outsource crucial type definitions like these",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.22,
          "end": 31.2,
          "en": "into separate files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.2,
          "end": 33.96,
          "en": "It's not a technical requirement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.96,
          "end": 36.09,
          "en": "as you can tell since everything works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.09,
          "end": 39,
          "en": "and it's also not something you have to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39,
          "end": 41.19,
          "en": "but it is a common pattern.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.19,
          "end": 43.983,
          "en": "And I'll start with this user type here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.91,
          "end": 48.495,
          "en": "You would typically create a separate file in the folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.495,
          "end": 52.38,
          "en": "to which this data model belongs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.38,
          "end": 54.21,
          "en": "So if you are describing a user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.21,
          "end": 56.943,
          "en": "it makes sense to be stored in the user folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.08,
          "end": 60.09,
          "en": "You would add a new file here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.09,
          "end": 64.92,
          "en": "and then typically name it user.model.ts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.92,
          "end": 68.691,
          "en": "And now you can simply cut this interface here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.691,
          "end": 70.8,
          "en": "this user interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.8,
          "end": 73.41,
          "en": "and also delete this commented out type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.41,
          "end": 74.53,
          "en": "since we don't need it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.81,
          "end": 79.383,
          "en": "and paste that interface into this user model file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.78999999999999,
          "end": 83.78999999999999,
          "en": "Now, in order to make it available outside of this file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.78999999999999,
          "end": 87.003,
          "en": "you also have to add the export keyword though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.05,
          "end": 90.78,
          "en": "And now with this, the advantage is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.78,
          "end": 94.71000000000001,
          "en": "that you can now easily use this type definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.71000000000001,
          "end": 96.453,
          "en": "in any file that needs it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.32,
          "end": 101.52000000000001,
          "en": "In this app, it is only that one user component file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.52000000000001,
          "end": 103.17,
          "en": "so it's not too important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.17,
          "end": 106.35,
          "en": "But if you were using that same data model,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.35,
          "end": 109.92,
          "en": "that same data type in different files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.92,
          "end": 113.94,
          "en": "defining it in a central place like this and exporting it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.94,
          "end": 115.77000000000001,
          "en": "simply make sure that you don't have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.77000000000001,
          "end": 119.25,
          "en": "to copy and paste type definitions around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.25,
          "end": 121.74,
          "en": "Therefore, now with that type being stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.74,
          "end": 123.18,
          "en": "in that extra file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.18,
          "end": 126.93,
          "en": "we have to import this user data definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.93,
          "end": 131.28,
          "en": "from ./user.model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.28,
          "end": 133.443,
          "en": "And with that, everything works again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.31,
          "end": 136.32,
          "en": "And that's also important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.32,
          "end": 138.48,
          "en": "When working with TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.48,
          "end": 141.32999999999998,
          "en": "you can import type definitions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.32999999999998,
          "end": 144.663,
          "en": "just as you can import classes and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.67000000000002,
          "end": 149.67000000000002,
          "en": "If you know that something is a type definition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.67000000000002,
          "end": 152.13,
          "en": "you can add the type keyword in front of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.13,
          "end": 153.78,
          "en": "to make that super clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.78,
          "end": 156.03,
          "en": "though technically this is not required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.03,
          "end": 158.16,
          "en": "But you might want to do that to make it very clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.16,
          "end": 161.793,
          "en": "that what we're importing here is just a type definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.649,
          "end": 167.55,
          "en": "And you can now do something similar for the task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.55,
          "end": 171.003,
          "en": "And you can of course also try doing this on your own first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.77,
          "end": 177.77,
          "en": "I will outsource it by again, grabbing this interface here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.65,
          "end": 182.46,
          "en": "so that it's not in the task component file anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 182.46,
          "end": 184.83,
          "en": "And now since I'm describing a task,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 184.83,
          "end": 188.61,
          "en": "I'll stay in this task sub folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.61,
          "end": 192.213,
          "en": "and in there I'll add a task.model.ts file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.29,
          "end": 194.82,
          "en": "And then just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 194.82,
          "end": 198.153,
          "en": "we put the interface in there and export it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 199.14,
          "end": 203.28,
          "en": "and now in the file where we need it, we can import it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.28,
          "end": 205.8,
          "en": "So here in the task component file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.8,
          "end": 210.8,
          "en": "we import this type task from ./task.model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 214.62,
          "end": 216.12,
          "en": "And again, as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.12,
          "end": 218.37,
          "en": "this is not something you have to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 218.37,
          "end": 220.05,
          "en": "but a common pattern you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.05,
          "end": 222.063,
          "en": "in many Angular applications.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
